## Adding new criteria later (you asked for this)

Open `index.html`, find the block marked **`METRIC REGISTRY — ADD NEW CRITERIA HERE`** near the top
of the script. Add one line:

```js
{k:'ev_ebitda', label:'EV/EBITDA', unit:'x', dec:1, grp:'Valuation'},
```

Filters, the column picker, sorting, CSV export and the detail view all pick it up automatically —
nothing else to change. If the number isn't in the dataset yet, add it to `compute_metrics()` in
`pipeline/build_data.py` too (and add a test in `pipeline/test_pipeline.py`).

**Or** define it purely in the app with a formula, no pipeline change at all:

```js
{k:'pat_per_cr_capex', label:'PAT per ₹Cr Capex', dec:2, grp:'Cash', hi:1,
  calc:c=>{const p=g(c,'pat'),x=g(c,'capex');return (p==null||!x)?null:p/x;}},
```

(Three metrics already work this way — see `off_high`, `up_low`, `ev`.)

